created: 2025-05-02, last updated: 2025-06-14, [Read more](https://github.com/pocketbase/pocketbase/discussions/6791)

If you want to read non-record submitted body fields you'll have to read them from the request.
```
core.RecordRequestEvent
```
embeds
```
core.RequestEvent
```
so all methods described in https://pocketbase.io/docs/go-routing/#reading-request-body should be available in the hook.
Or in other words, you can do something like:
```
// v1.
read/scan the request body fields into a typed struct
data := struct {
Invite string `json:"invite" form:"invite"`
}{}
if err := e.BindBody(&data); err != nil {
return e.BadRequestError("Failed to read request data", err)
}
println(data.Invite)

